polardbx_hasher(id1, id2, id3, id4, id5, id6, id7, id8, id9, id10, id11, id12)
-8228158238384414951
#
# Test 12: Test error case with out of range hash value
#
Create a test case where we can verify the out of range error
We'll use a very narrow range that should fail for most values
CREATE TABLE t9 (
id INT PRIMARY KEY,
data VARCHAR(50)
);
INSERT INTO t9 VALUES (1, 'test_data');
This should fail if the hash value is outside the narrow range
Using a range that's unlikely to contain the hash value
SELECT polardbx_hasher(id, 100, 200) FROM t9 WHERE id = 1;
ERROR HY000: Hash value 6161172798010463909 computed from partitioning key [id=1] is out of the expected source partition range [100, 200]. This indicates a data consistency issue during partition migration.
